{
  "configuration_id": "config_012",
  "reason": "The strongest signal from completed experiments is that pca_n2000 dramatically outperforms scgpt as the RNA encoder (0.5353 vs 0.4348 in multimodal concat). However, we do not yet know how much of config_049's performance comes from the image modality versus the RNA encoder alone. With scgpt, image added only ~2.4 points (0.4348 multimodal vs 0.4106 RNA-only), but with pca_n2000 the picture may be very different. config_012 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_049 that isolates the image contribution. If RNA alone approaches ~0.50+, the image modality is marginal and future budget should focus on RNA encoder/aggregation choices; if RNA alone is ~0.40, image is contributing ~13 points and investing in image encoder, multiprofile aggregation, or fusion becomes critical. This single experiment resolves the most important architectural uncertainty and will efficiently guide all subsequent design decisions under the limited budget."
}

